  "status_text": "For a whole class of graphs it is now checked that a circuit without NOT gates needs about as many gates as it has input wires. If no row lies inside all the others and no column inside all the others, every AND/OR circuit of fan-in two for an n by m graph, n and m at least 2, on one-a-side inputs has at least n + m - 1 gates [L-meta-19383]; the checked floor with NOT gates counts only rows and columns outside the largest groups of equal ones [L-meta-19361]. And a second 5 by 5 graph shows a saving of at least four: at most 7 with NOT gates [L-meta-19447], at least 11 without [L-meta-10135].",
